From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antonin Tomecek <antonin@jupiter.localdomain>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:01:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libalpm: no caller callbacks in the forked child of
 _alpm_run_chroot

_alpm_handle_free() in the child (before execv of a scriptlet or hook)
logs through the caller's log callback. Callbacks of a language binding
are not meant to run in a forked child: the LSL runtime of the LuxOS
package manager aborts a callback from another thread id, so the child
died and the scriptlet or hook did not run. Clear the callbacks first,
like the download sandbox child does.
---
 lib/libalpm/util.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/libalpm/util.c b/lib/libalpm/util.c
index 6739161..9512ebb 100644
--- a/lib/libalpm/util.c
+++ b/lib/libalpm/util.c
@@ -694,6 +694,15 @@ int _alpm_run_chroot(alpm_handle_t *handle, const char *cmd, char *const argv[],
 		unsetenv("BASH_ENV");
 		umask(0022);
 		_alpm_reset_signals();
+		/* the callbacks belong to the parent process: a language binding may not
+		 * be able to run in the forked child (the LSL runtime aborts a callback
+		 * from another thread id), and _alpm_handle_free() logs */
+		alpm_option_set_logcb(handle, NULL, NULL);
+		alpm_option_set_dlcb(handle, NULL, NULL);
+		alpm_option_set_fetchcb(handle, NULL, NULL);
+		alpm_option_set_eventcb(handle, NULL, NULL);
+		alpm_option_set_questioncb(handle, NULL, NULL);
+		alpm_option_set_progresscb(handle, NULL, NULL);
 		_alpm_handle_free(handle);
 		execv(cmd, argv);
 		/* execv only returns if there was an error */
-- 
